binary: build/mix-final-actual_artefacts/Release/mix-final-actual.exe
{"id":1,"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":{"capabilities":{"tools":{}},"instructions":"Mixes a folder of audio tracks on a real mixing console. You never hear audio: each turn the console measures the mix and sends you a text report and its console tools; you answer with tool calls. Workflow: open_session(folder) starts the console and its first mix; then loop: next_turn -> read the turn (follow its SYSTEM part, use only its TOOLS) -> post_note 2-4 short notes while you work (what you read in the measurements, then your plan; the user watches them live in the mixer page) -> submit_turn with ALL of the turn's tool calls in one call. The first mix is 5 turns; then the mixer page opens in the user's browser. After that, keep calling next_turn: requests the user types in the page arrive as new turns. Stop when the user says they are done (close_session ends the console). The console keeps running when you stop; list_projects shows earlier mixes, and open_session reopens one as it was.","protocolVersion":"2025-06-18","serverInfo":{"name":"mix-final-actual","version":"0.1.0"}}}
{"id":2,"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":{"tools":[{"description":"Start the console on a folder of tracks (WAV/AIFF/FLAC, one file per track, file names = track names such as 'Lead Vocal.wav'). Starts the first mix, which waits for your turns; a folder with a saved project reopens it instead (live at once). Reuses the session if it is already open.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"folder":{"description":"Absolute path of the tracks folder.","type":"string"},"new_mix":{"description":"Start over with a new first mix even if the folder has a saved project (default false: a saved project is reopened as it was).","type":"boolean"},"turns":{"description":"Turns in the first mix (default 5).","type":"integer"}},"required":["folder"],"type":"object"},"name":"open_session"},{"description":"Wait for the console's next turn and return it: a SYSTEM part (how to mix, how to answer), a USER part (this turn's measurements, your recent turns and their effect, the user's request if any) and the TOOLS (function schemas). Returns 'no turn' if none arrives within wait_seconds; call it again to keep waiting.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"folder":{"description":"Absolute path of the tracks folder (one audio file per track, named by instrument). Optional when only one session is open.","type":"string"},"wait_seconds":{"description":"Up to 50 (default 45).","type":"number"}},"required":[],"type":"object"},"name":"next_turn"},{"description":"Answer a turn: content = the reply text the turn's SYSTEM part asks for; tool_calls = every console tool call of this turn, in order, each {name, arguments} following the turn's TOOLS schemas. One call per turn.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"content":{"type":"string"},"folder":{"description":"Absolute path of the tracks folder (one audio file per track, named by instrument). Optional when only one session is open.","type":"string"},"tool_calls":{"items":{"properties":{"arguments":{"type":"object"},"name":{"type":"string"}},"required":["name"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"turn":{"description":"The turn id from next_turn.","type":"integer"}},"required":["turn","content","tool_calls"],"type":"object"},"name":"submit_turn"},{"description":"Post a short note on the turn you are working on (one or two sentences: what you read in the measurements, what you plan to change and why). The user sees it at once in the mixer page while you work, like watching you think. Post 2-4 per turn, before submit_turn; it does not change the mix.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"folder":{"description":"Absolute path of the tracks folder (one audio file per track, named by instrument). Optional when only one session is open.","type":"string"},"text":{"description":"The note (plain text, up to 2000 characters).","type":"string"},"turn":{"description":"The turn id from next_turn.","type":"integer"}},"required":["turn","text"],"type":"object"},"name":"post_note"},{"description":"Where the session is: first mix (turn k of n), or live with the page URL.","inputSchema":{"properties":{"folder":{"description":"Absolute path of the tracks folder (one audio file per track, named by instrument). Optional when only one session is open.","type":"string"}},"required":[],"type":"object"},"name":"session_status"},{"description":"The mixes opened lately (newest first): folder, name, when, and the page URL if its console is running. To work on one again, call open_session with its folder (a saved project reopens as it was).","inputSchema":{"properties":{},"required":[],"type":"object"},"name":"list_projects"},{"description":"Stop the console for a folder (the page stops working).","inputSchema":{"properties":{"folder":{"description":"Absolute path of the tracks folder (one audio file per track, named by instrument). Optional when only one session is open.","type":"string"}},"required":[],"type":"object"},"name":"close_session"}]}}
